D. Experiment Procedure
After reading and signing the consent form, the participants would have a training trial on how to use the three interactions. They were given a verbal description on the interaction usage. Once the participants felt confident on how to use the interactions, they would have an 8km driving practice to familiarize themselves with driving in the simulator. Each interaction would be experienced at least once during this practice trial.
When the drivers were familiar with driving in the simulator using the interactions, the effect of the interactions on their driving performance and eye movement behavior would then be examined. The test urban road was with three lanes in each direction with a speed limitation of 80 km/h. The traffic density was set to 500 vehicles per lane per hour with their speeds ranging from 50 to 80 km/h. The participants were instructed to follow a leading vehicle in the middle lane without changing lanes. Each interaction was tested three times. All the 9 LBS tasks (3 interactions x 3 times each) were randomly arranged in the test trial. The time gap between each two adjacent LBS tasks was about 90 s.
