B. Eye Movement
To intuitively illustrate the road center area, the fixations fell within this area were marked with a dark red color, while the other fixations were marked with dark blue. See Figure 7. No significant differences were found in the attention allocation in the road center areas when using different interactions. The coordinate of the road center point is presented in Table IV. The RFCPs when using None, PPU, BT+AUD and BT+HUD were 77.6%, 86.5%, 87.4% and 82.9%, respectively. The lowest RFCP in the None interaction group indicates that drivers with a low workload would divide their attention more to the other areas. However, when there was a NDRT that required a relatively higher workload, drivers would concentrate more in the road center area to keep aware of the forward road traffic for safety reasons.
